    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194">

                <pb facs="0367" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/333: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-15T18:00:00-05:00">December 15, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Reference is made to your telegram of December 15, 8 a.m., No. 74.<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d194-f1"/> We are prepared, subject to an advance agreement
                    regarding <pb facs="0368" n="272" xml:id="pg272"/> a satisfactory communiqué, to
                    accede to the British idea of bringing the present conversations to an end
                    through a tripartite meeting on December 19 or 20. That time will be close
                    enough to the Japanese denunciation to render the connection between the two
                    events clear in the mind of the public without the necessity of its being
                    stressed openly. Our meeting the British on this basis should render it easier
                    for them to meet us in our preoccupations concerning the communiqué’s
                    contents.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
